  "id": "Compound::DB04868 - Disease::DOID:2531",
  "verbalization": "Nilotinib is associated with Hematologic Cancer through multiple pathways that involve the inhibition of Bcr-Abl and the use of Antineoplastic Agents. The evidence suggests that Nilotinib, through its role as a Bcr-Abl inhibitor, may contribute to the treatment of Hematologic Cancer by targeting the underlying molecular mechanisms of the disease. Additionally, Nilotinib is linked to the reduction of Blood Albumin and Blood Glucose levels, which are further treated by Nelarabine, an Antineoplastic Agent. These pathways highlight the complex interplay between Nilotinib and the treatment of Hematologic Cancer, with the shared ancestry of Nilotinib and Nelarabine pointing to a common biological context. The integration of these pathways suggests that Nilotinib may exert its therapeutic effects through multiple mechanisms, potentially enhancing the efficacy of treatments targeting Hematologic Cancer.",
